Task 1 – Step-by-Step Spotify Playlist Creation
Objective

The purpose of this task is to create a structured prompt that instructs ChatGPT to explain a process step-by-step and provide the answer in bullet points.

A structured prompt makes it easier for the AI to understand:

What task needs to be completed
What steps should be explained
How detailed the response should be
What format the response should follow
Prompt

Act as a Spotify expert and explain how to create a new playlist on Spotify. Give me a simple step-by-step guide that a beginner can easily understand. Start from opening Spotify and end with saving the playlist successfully. Explain each major step in the correct order. Mention important options such as naming the playlist, adding a description, choosing a cover image if available, and adding songs. Present the entire answer using bullet points. Keep the instructions practical and easy to follow. Do not add unnecessary information.

Example Output
How to Create a New Playlist on Spotify
Open Spotify
Open the Spotify application on your phone or computer.
Log in to your Spotify account.
Go to Your Library
Open Your Library from the Spotify menu.
Look for the option to create a new playlist.
Create a New Playlist
Select Create Playlist or the corresponding option.
A new playlist will be created.
Name Your Playlist
Enter a suitable name for your playlist.
For example: My Workout Songs or Chill Evening Playlist.
Add a Description
Add a short description if you want.
This can explain the purpose or theme of your playlist.
Add Songs
Select Add Songs.
Search for songs, artists, albums, or podcasts.
Select the songs you want to include.
Arrange Your Playlist
Check the added songs.
Reorder or remove songs if required.
Customize the Playlist
Add or change the playlist cover image if the option is available.
Save and Use the Playlist
Spotify automatically saves playlist changes.
You can now play, share, or continue adding songs to the playlist.
What I Learned

This task demonstrates that adding instructions such as "step-by-step," "beginner-friendly," and "use bullet points" gives the AI a much more organized output.

Task 2 – Zomato vs Swiggy Comparison
Objective

The objective is to create a prompt that tells ChatGPT to compare two services and present the information in a table format.

A table is useful for comparisons because the same features can be viewed side-by-side.

Prompt

Compare Zomato and Swiggy as food-delivery platforms in India. Compare their commonly available features and services, including restaurant discovery, food ordering, delivery tracking, offers and discounts, subscription/membership benefits, restaurant ratings and reviews, customer support, and payment options. Present the answer in a table with exactly these columns: Feature, Zomato, Swiggy. Keep the descriptions short and easy to understand. Do not declare an overall winner; simply explain the differences between the two platforms.